WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.137
Unit 2 is identity and cloud-app signals.

2
00:00:03.137 --> 00:00:07.424
Defender for Identity's sensors go
on domain controllers, A D F S,

3
00:00:07.424 --> 00:00:12.865
A D C S and Entra Connect servers, and
Defender for Cloud Apps' connectors bring in

4
00:00:12.865 --> 00:00:18.388
software-as-a-service behavior, so both
land in the same incidents as the endpoint.

5
00:00:18.388 --> 00:00:22.156
Pilot the sensors on one domain
controller per domain first;

6
00:00:22.156 --> 00:00:25.850
domain controllers remain Tier
zero until they're retired.

7
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:30.703
Microsoft Learn's government page
for Defender for Identity gives

8
00:00:30.703 --> 00:00:34.950
the sensor endpoint for G C C, a
G C C address, or the service tag.

9
00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:40.226
Learn also says new features reach G C C
within ninety days of commercial release,

10
00:00:40.226 --> 00:00:42.825
and previews may not be supported there.

11
00:00:42.825 --> 00:00:43.938
Then the gaps.

12
00:00:43.938 --> 00:00:48.727
Learn's Cloud Apps government page
lists App Governance's predefined

13
00:00:48.727 --> 00:00:53.350
policy alerts and threat-detection
alerts as roadmap items for G C C.

14
00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:56.546
And Learn's advanced
hunting schema says Cloud

15
00:00:56.546 --> 00:00:59.250
Apps behaviors aren't available for G C C.

16
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:04.585
The interim path for O auth app abuse is
the application detections in Sentinel,

17
00:01:04.585 --> 00:01:07.800
in the Security Operations
and Telemetry book.
